   "id": "5fea2d7b44c7fa67",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Overview: Malignant subtype analysis based on inferred meta-interactions in the HGSOC dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook analyzes **malignant-cell heterogeneity** in the **HGSOC spatial transcriptomics dataset** using the **meta-interactions (MIs)** inferred by **SpiderNet**. Rather than relying only on gene-expression clustering, the analysis integrates **MI activity**, **spatial organization**, **subtype-associated molecular programs**, and **in silico perturbation analysis** to identify and interpret distinct malignant states.\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook mainly performs the following analyses:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Load processed data and the malignant-cell subset**  \n",
    "   Read the processed HGSOC data, extract **malignant cells** and their associated metadata, and prepare the inputs needed for subtype-level downstream analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Quantify malignant-cell MI activity**  \n",
    "   Use the inferred **MI loadings** to characterize how strongly each malignant cell is associated with different interaction programs, providing an **interaction-informed representation** of tumor-cell states.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Identify malignant subtypes**  \n",
    "   Cluster malignant cells based on molecular and/or **MI-derived features**, then define subtype labels to capture the major malignant populations within the tumor.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Characterize subtype-specific molecular, interaction, and spatial features**  \n",
    "   Examine **marker genes**, **biological programs**, **MI activity patterns**, and **spatial organization** associated with each subtype, and visualize these results using embeddings, subtype-level summaries, and **MI-high versus MI-low comparisons**.\n",
    "\n",
    "5. **Perform in silico perturbation analysis to probe subtype-associated signaling programs**  \n",
    "   Select representative **sender–receiver interaction programs**, perturb prioritized **ligand–receptor (LR) pairs** in silico, and evaluate the predicted effects on **malignant-cell gene-expression responses**, **log2 fold changes**, and downstream subtype-associated molecular patterns.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, this notebook provides an **MI-guided framework** for dissecting **malignant-cell subtypes** in HGSOC and linking tumor heterogeneity to **interaction programs**, **molecular signatures**, **spatial organization**, and **predicted in-silico perturbation responses**."
   ]
  },
